example CtaSectionGallery {
  id: "@community/example-gallery-cta-sections"
  version: "1.0.0"

  domain: frontend-design
  description: "17 curated CTA section screenshots from Land-book Pro, tagged by pattern type and persona lean. CTA sections are inflection points in the scroll narrative — they ask the visitor to make a decision. They appear in two primary positions: mid-page (as momentum checkpoints) and end-of-page (as the final conversion moment)."

  observations: [
    "B2B products almost always offer a 'book a demo' or 'talk to sales' path, not a self-serve signup. GTM Analytics, Pontera, V7-Go, Happyrobot, and Rhetorich all funnel to a consultation or demo rather than a free trial. The CTA copy is qualified ('for enterprises,' 'for finance teams') which intentionally filters out low-intent visitors. Self-serve signups (base44, bright-os in the wider gallery) use low-friction copy like 'get started free.'",
    "Developer-facing CTAs treat code as the conversion action. Codegen and Inertiajs frame their CTAs around code actions: an install command, a GitHub star, a documentation link. The button is present but secondary to the code metaphor. This signals comfort with the developer audience — they trust the visitor to execute independently.",
    "Dual-path CTAs appear when a product serves two distinct audiences. Cardless (developer vs. business), Modern Vendor Financing (apply vs. partner), and Veo (shop vs. trial) all use two equally weighted actions. This is preferable to forcing one audience's path on another. The visual treatment is typically two side-by-side buttons: one primary (filled), one secondary (outlined or ghost).",
    "Trust signals adjacent to the CTA reduce conversion anxiety. GTM Analytics, Pontera, and Modern Vendor Financing all place company logos, compliance badges, or social proof immediately below or above the CTA button. This pattern is especially common in fintech and enterprise — the implicit message is 'other credible organizations already made this decision.'",
    "Emotional and wellness products use soft persuasion, never urgency. Dawn AI's CTA uses reassurance-oriented copy; no countdown timers, no 'limited time' framing. This is consistent with the warm-institutional and editorial personas — urgency tactics would damage brand trust in sensitive categories (mental health, wellness, healthcare).",
  ]

  items: [
    {
      file: "aira--ai-sales-agent-for-sales-teams.webp"
      pattern: "dark end-page CTA + large headline + single primary button + AI brand"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "High-contrast dark section; CTA echoes hero language; minimal decoration"
    },
    {
      file: "athleats--healthy-performance-driven-recipes-for-athl.webp"
      pattern: "lifestyle photography CTA + bold call to action + app download prompt"
      persona_lean: [warm-institutional, editorial]
      notes: "Full-bleed food photo as CTA backdrop; clear app store badges"
    },
    {
      file: "cardless--embedded-credit-card-platform.webp"
      pattern: "B2B partnership CTA + dual-audience copy + centered layout"
      persona_lean: [swiss-modernist, dense-pragmatist]
      notes: "Two-path CTA (developer vs. business); fintech tone; clean split"
    },
    {
      file: "cernel-product-onboarding-for-ecommerce-teams.webp"
      pattern: "mid-page CTA banner + reduced friction copy + ecommerce context"
      persona_lean: [warm-institutional, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Inline rather than full-section; 'get started' without pricing commitment"
    },
    {
      file: "client-challenge.webp"
      pattern: "minimal typographic CTA + single line + maximum whitespace"
      persona_lean: [tokyo-minimal, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Extreme restraint; one sentence + one button; nothing else"
    },
    {
      file: "codegen--the-os-for-code-agents.webp"
      pattern: "developer CTA + code-adjacent headline + dark theme + OSS install prompt"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "npm/brew install framed as the CTA; developer community tone"
    },
    {
      file: "dawn-ai-for-mental-health--247-support-for-your-mind.webp"
      pattern: "soft gradient CTA + emotional reassurance copy + single CTA button"
      persona_lean: [warm-institutional, editorial]
      notes: "Gentle persuasion; no urgency pressure; safe/supportive tone"
    },
    {
      file: "gtm-analytics--equals.webp"
      pattern: "data-product CTA + demo request + trust signals row"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "'Book a demo' primary; company logos as trust anchors below CTA"
    },
    {
      file: "happyrobot--ai-workers-handle-end-to-end-tasks-at-scal.webp"
      pattern: "AI infrastructure CTA + workflow diagram visual + enterprise framing"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist]
      notes: "Enterprise AI; process diagram reinforces CTA; 'talk to sales' path"
    },
    {
      file: "inertiajs.webp"
      pattern: "OSS CTA + GitHub star prompt + documentation link + developer"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Open-source product; GitHub and docs are the two CTA actions"
    },
    {
      file: "interfere--build-software-that-never-breaks.webp"
      pattern: "bold statement CTA + large type + single action + dark bg"
      persona_lean: [brutalist-expressive, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Statement-as-CTA approach; typography is the visual; button is secondary"
    },
    {
      file: "keytail--be-the-answer-everywhere-people-search.webp"
      pattern: "search-bar CTA + low-friction sign-up + centered"
      persona_lean: [warm-institutional]
      notes: "Search-input as signup form; reduces perceived effort; product metaphor"
    },
    {
      file: "modern-vendor-financing-for-b2b-software-and-hardware-p.webp"
      pattern: "fintech CTA + dual path (apply/partner) + trust badge row"
      persona_lean: [swiss-modernist, dense-pragmatist]
      notes: "Two distinct audiences; compliance/trust signals visible; conservative"
    },
    {
      file: "pontera--infrastructure-for-modern-connected-retireme.webp"
      pattern: "B2B platform CTA + ROI framing + schedule demo"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Business outcome language; ROI/metric teaser before CTA button"
    },
    {
      file: "rhetorich--make-speaking-your-firms-most-powerful-adv.webp"
      pattern: "professional services CTA + consultation framing + authority tone"
      persona_lean: [swiss-modernist, editorial]
      notes: "'Book a consultation' as primary; positions as premium service"
    },
    {
      file: "v7-go--ai-agent-platform-for-finance-legal--insuranc.webp"
      pattern: "enterprise AI CTA + industry-specific copy + dark SaaS"
      persona_lean: [dense-pragmatist, swiss-modernist]
      notes: "Finance/legal vertical framing; compliance-aware copy; enterprise gate"
    },
    {
      file: "veo-sports-cameras--record-stream-and-analyse.webp"
      pattern: "hardware product CTA + action photography + shop/try framing"
      persona_lean: [warm-institutional, editorial]
      notes: "Physical product; photography-led; dual path (shop vs. free trial)"
    },
  ]

  base_path: "resources/landbook/sections-cta"

  persona_mapping: {
    "dense-pragmatist": ["aira--ai-sales-agent-for-sales-teams", "codegen--the-os-for-code-agents", "gtm-analytics--equals", "happyrobot--ai-workers-handle-end-to-end-tasks-at-scal", "v7-go--ai-agent-platform-for-finance-legal--insuranc", "pontera--infrastructure-for-modern-connected-retireme"]
    "swiss-modernist": ["cardless--embedded-credit-card-platform", "client-challenge", "inertiajs", "modern-vendor-financing-for-b2b-software-and-hardware-p", "rhetorich--make-speaking-your-firms-most-powerful-adv"]
    "warm-institutional": ["athleats--healthy-performance-driven-recipes-for-athl", "cernel-product-onboarding-for-ecommerce-teams", "dawn-ai-for-mental-health--247-support-for-your-mind", "keytail--be-the-answer-everywhere-people-search", "veo-sports-cameras--record-stream-and-analyse"]
    "editorial": ["athleats--healthy-performance-driven-recipes-for-athl", "dawn-ai-for-mental-health--247-support-for-your-mind", "rhetorich--make-speaking-your-firms-most-powerful-adv", "veo-sports-cameras--record-stream-and-analyse"]
    "brutalist-expressive": ["interfere--build-software-that-never-breaks"]
    "tokyo-minimal": ["client-challenge"]
  }

  agent_workflow: """
    1. Determine CTA position first: mid-page checkpoint or final end-page conversion. Mid-page CTAs (cernel, keytail) are lower-friction and shorter. End-page CTAs (aira, interfere, client-challenge) carry the full conversion weight of the page.
    2. Match copy mode to product category. Enterprise/B2B: outcome framing + demo path. Developer: code action + secondary button. Consumer/wellness: reassurance copy + single clear action. Hardware: photography + dual path.
    3. Use trust signal samples when the product is high-stakes. GTM Analytics and Modern Vendor Financing demonstrate how to surround a CTA with credibility signals without making the section visually noisy. 4-6 muted logos below the button is the standard execution.
    4. Cross-reference pricing for dual-path logic. The dual-path CTA pattern often mirrors pricing tier logic — understanding how the product segments buyers in the pricing gallery helps write the right two CTA labels.
    5. End-page CTAs should echo hero language. Aira's end-page CTA mirrors its hero headline. This creates a narrative loop. When selecting a CTA sample, check if the hero sample (from the hero gallery) uses compatible language patterns.
  """

  related: [
    @community/example-gallery-hero-sections,
    @community/example-gallery-pricing-sections,
    @community/example-gallery-full-landings,
  ]
}
